IMPORT prelude

-- Medicare Levy Act 1986 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- how much Medicare levy I pay: s 3 (threshold amount, phase-in limit,
-- the married-person rules in s 3(3) and (3A), private patient hospital cover in s 3(5)), s 3A (tier 2 and tier 3 earners, with
-- the Private Health Insurance Act 2007 s 22-30 tables as s 3A(3) modifies them), s 6(1) (the 2% rate), s 7(1) and (2) (no levy
-- on small incomes, and the 10% shading-in), s 8 (families: no levy under the family income threshold, the reduction above it,
-- the spouse apportionment and the pass-over of an unused reduction to the spouse), ss 8B, 8C and 8D (the Medicare levy
-- surcharge for a person without private patient hospital cover, single, single with dependants, or married), and s 9 (part of
-- the year a prescribed person).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- the individual on whose taxable income the levy is imposed. Every exported question is phrased as that
-- person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 53, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 58, 2026 (Register id
-- C2026C00295), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03351.txt. The low-income figures are in the Act's own text
-- (ss 3, 8, 8D), amended each year by an amending Act; no instrument sets them. Also used: Private Health Insurance Act 2007
-- ss 22-30, 22-35, 22-40, 22-45 and 45-1, as deposited at
-- ../../../private-health-insurance-act-2007/registers/source-bundle/C2007A00031.txt.
--
-- THE YEAR THE FIGURES ARE FOR. The compilation states each figure once, with no year: "$28,011", "$35,013", "$44,268",
-- "$55,335", "$47,238", "$4,338", "$61,623". The amendment history shows ss 3, 8 and 8D amended in each recent year, last by
-- Act No. 58, 2026, commencing 1 July 2026. INFERENCE (not stated in the deposit): these are the figures for the 2025-26 year
-- of income, and they stand for later years until amended. For the 2024-25 year of income and earlier, every money answer here
-- is `Not in the deposited text`. The s 6 rate of 2% is asked separately and carries no year.
--
-- THE DEPOSIT DROPS EVERY FORMULA set as an image ("in accordance with the formula:" is followed by nothing): the s 8(2)
-- reduction formula and the part-year surcharge formulas in ss 8B(2)(b), 8C(3)(b) and 8D(4). So the s 8(2) reduction is an
-- INPUT, and a part-year surcharge is `Not in the deposited text`. The Private Health Insurance Act's tier thresholds are
-- indexed under its s 22-45 and the indexed figures are not deposited, so they are INPUTS; its s 22-40(4) increase for two or
-- more children is a formula the deposit also drops, and is an INPUT.
--
-- A year of income is named by the calendar year in which it begins: 2025 is the 2025-26 year of income.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 6(2)-(6), s 7(3)-(4), ss 8E-8G and s 10 (trustees, and the surcharge on beneficiaries' trust income: the seat
-- is the individual taxpayer, not the trustee); s 9A (lump sums in arrears -- the person with such a sum is told their case is
-- `Not covered by this encoding`); the s 5 note's offset for surcharge on lump sums (ITAA 1997 Subdiv 61-L); ss 1, 2, 4, 5, 11
-- (machinery). Rounding is not modelled. Borrowed terms are asked as facts: "married" and "spouse" (Part VIIB of the 1936
-- Act), "dependant" (ss 251R, 251V), "prescribed person" (s 251U), "income for surcharge purposes" (ITAA 1997), entitlement to
-- the s 160AAAA rebate, the Subdiv 61-A offset and the Subdiv 961-A and 961-B notional offsets, and family tax benefit.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. Consistent with ../../../income-tax-rates-act-1986/encodings/baseline-2026-10 and
-- ../../../income-tax-assessment-act-1997/encodings/baseline-2026-10, which leave the levy to this Act. See NOTES.md.

§ `Medicare Levy Act 1986 -- the levy and the surcharge`

§§ `Answers and helpers`

-- Every money answer is either an amount, or says plainly that the deposited compilation has no rule for the case, or that
-- the case is one this encoding leaves out.
DECLARE Answer IS ONE OF
    Amount HAS `value` IS A NUMBER
    `Not in the deposited text`
    `Not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `Which year the deposited figures are for`

-- See the header: INFERENCE that the compilation's figures are those for 2025-26 and later.
@export Does the deposited text give the Medicare levy low-income figures for my year of income?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which your year of income begins (2025 for 2025-26)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the deposited text give the figures for my year` IF `year` AT LEAST 2025

§§ `s 6 -- the rate of levy`

-- s 6(1): "The rate of levy payable by a person upon a taxable income is 2%." (Gloss: the levy is a flat 2% of taxable income,
-- before the small-income, family, prescribed-person and surcharge rules.)
@export What is the rate of Medicare levy on my taxable income, in percent (s 6(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the rate of levy` IS 2

@export How much is 2% of my taxable income, before any small-income or family relief (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the levy at the full rate` IS
    `the greater of` `taxable income` 0 TIMES `What is the rate of levy` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `s 3 -- threshold amount and phase-in limit`

-- s 3(1): "threshold amount means: (a) for a person who is entitled to a rebate under section 160AAAA of the Assessment Act --
-- $44,268; or (c) in any other case -- $28,011." "phase-in limit means: (a) for a person who is entitled to a rebate under
-- section 160AAAA of the Assessment Act -- $55,335; or (c) in any other case -- $35,013." (Gloss: the s 160AAAA rebate is the
-- seniors and pensioners rebate of the 1936 Act; whether I am entitled to it is asked as a fact.)
@export What is my Medicare levy threshold amount, in dollars (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the seniors and pensioners rebate under s 160AAAA of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my threshold amount` IS
    IF `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` THEN 44268 ELSE 28011

@export What is my Medicare levy phase-in limit, in dollars (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the seniors and pensioners rebate under s 160AAAA of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my phase-in limit` IS
    IF `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` THEN 55335 ELSE 35013

§§ `s 7 -- small incomes`

-- s 7(1): "Where the taxable income of a person does not exceed the threshold amount, no levy is payable by the person upon that
-- taxable income."
@export Is my income small enough that I pay no Medicare levy (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year, in dollars
      `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the seniors and pensioners rebate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my income under the threshold` IF
    `taxable income` AT MOST `What is my threshold amount` `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate`

-- s 7(2): "Where the taxable income of a person exceeds the threshold amount but does not exceed the phase-in limit, the amount
-- of levy payable by the person upon that taxable income but for sections 8 and 9 shall not exceed 10% of the amount of the
-- excess." (Gloss: the shading-in -- between the two figures the levy is the lesser of 2% of the income and 10% of the excess.)
@export How much Medicare levy do I pay on my own income, before the family, prescribed-person and surcharge rules (ss 6, 7)?
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year, in dollars
      `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the seniors and pensioners rebate
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much levy on my own income` IS
    IF `Is my income under the threshold` `taxable income` `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `taxable income` AT MOST `What is my phase-in limit` `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate`
         THEN `the lesser of` (`How much is the levy at the full rate` `taxable income`)
                              ((`taxable income` MINUS `What is my threshold amount` `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate`) TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100)
         ELSE `How much is the levy at the full rate` `taxable income`

§§ `s 3(3) -- married on the last day of the year`

-- s 3(3): "(a) a person shall be deemed not to be married to another person if they are living separately and apart; and (b)
-- where the last person to whom another person was married during a year of income died during the year of income, those
-- persons shall be deemed to have been married on the last day of the year of income." "Married" itself is the 1936 Act's
-- Part VIIB term (s 3(4)) and is asked as a fact.
@export Am I treated as married on the last day of the year of income, for the Medicare levy (s 3(3))?
GIVEN `had a spouse on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married (as Part VIIB of the 1936 Act reads it) on 30 June
      `living separately and apart from that spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and that spouse were living separately and apart
      `spouse died during the year while we were married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the last person you were married to in the year died during the year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I married on the last day of the year` IF
       (`had a spouse on the last day of the year` AND (NOT `living separately and apart from that spouse`))
    OR `spouse died during the year while we were married`

§§ `The facts one taxpayer states for one year of income`

-- For the surcharge (ss 8B-8D), which section applies depends on whether, "during the whole of the period", the person is
-- married and has dependants. The person states the pattern across the year, after s 3(3)(a) (living apart) and s 3(3A) (a
-- spouse who died is treated as a spouse until 30 June).
DECLARE `Marriage in the year` IS ONE OF
    `married all year`
    `not married at any time in the year`
    `married for part of the year`

DECLARE `Dependants in the year` IS ONE OF
    `dependants all year`
    `no dependants at any time in the year`
    `dependants for part of the year`

DECLARE Taxpayer HAS
    `year of income begins` IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an eligible lump sum in arrears` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a spouse on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `living separately and apart from that spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `spouse died during the year while we were married` IS A BOOLEAN
    `spouse's taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `spouse would be liable to levy but for ss 8 and 9` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to a Subdivision 61-A offset for my child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to a Subdivision 961-B notional offset` IS A BOOLEAN
    `people counted for the family income threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `of them, people for whom family tax benefit was payable to me` IS A NUMBER
    `reduction worked out by the s 8(2) formula` IS A NUMBER
    `days in the year of income` IS A NUMBER
    `days I was a prescribed person` IS A NUMBER
    `marriage in the year` IS A `Marriage in the year`
    `dependants in the year` IS A `Dependants in the year`
    `days on which I or a dependant had no private patient hospital cover` IS A NUMBER
    `income for surcharge purposes` IS A NUMBER
    `spouse's income for surcharge purposes` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 1 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`p is married on the last day` MEANS
    `Am I married on the last day of the year` (`p`'s `had a spouse on the last day of the year`)
                                               (`p`'s `living separately and apart from that spouse`)
                                               (`p`'s `spouse died during the year while we were married`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's levy on own income` MEANS
    `How much levy on my own income` (`p`'s `taxable income`) (`p`'s `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate`)

§§ `s 8 -- a person who has a spouse or dependants`

-- s 8(1): "Where a person: (a) is a married person on the last day of the year of income; or (b) is entitled to a tax offset
-- under Subdivision 61-A of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 for the year of income in respect of the person's child ...; or
-- (c) is entitled to a notional tax offset under Subdivision 961-B of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 for the year of income;
-- and the family income in relation to the person does not exceed the family income threshold in relation to the person, no
-- levy is payable by the person upon the taxable income of the person." (Gloss: the family case. Subdiv 61-A is the dependent
-- (invalid and carer) tax offset; Subdiv 961-B a notional offset; both asked as facts.)
@export Am I in the family case for the Medicare levy (s 8(1)(a)-(c))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in the family case` IF
       `p is married on the last day` `p`
    OR `p`'s `entitled to a Subdivision 61-A offset for my child`
    OR `p`'s `entitled to a Subdivision 961-B notional offset`

-- s 8(5): "family income ... means: (a) if the person was a married person on the last day of the year of income -- the sum of
-- the taxable income of the person and the taxable income of the spouse of the person; and (b) in any other case -- the taxable
-- income of the person."
@export What is my family income for the Medicare levy, in dollars (s 8(5))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my family income` IS
    IF `p is married on the last day` `p`
    THEN `p`'s `taxable income` PLUS `p`'s `spouse's taxable income`
    ELSE `p`'s `taxable income`

-- s 8(5): "family income threshold ... means $47,238 increased by $4,338 for each person covered by paragraph 961-5(1)(c) of
-- the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 in respect of whom ... the relevant person or the spouse ... is entitled to a notional tax
-- offset under Subdivision 961-A". s 8(6): for a person not married on the last day, the $47,238 "shall not be increased on
-- account of another person unless family tax benefit ... was payable to the first-mentioned person in respect of that other
-- person". s 8(7): for a person entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate, "each reference to $47,238 were a reference to $61,623".
@export What is my family income threshold for the Medicare levy, in dollars (s 8(5)-(7))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my family income threshold` IS
    (IF `p`'s `entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate` THEN 61623 ELSE 47238)
    PLUS 4338 TIMES (IF `p is married on the last day` `p`
                     THEN `p`'s `people counted for the family income threshold`
                     ELSE `the lesser of` (`p`'s `people counted for the family income threshold`)
                                          (`p`'s `of them, people for whom family tax benefit was payable to me`))

@export Is our family income small enough that I pay no Medicare levy (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our family income under the family threshold` IF
        `Am I in the family case` `p`
    AND `What is my family income` `p` AT MOST `What is my family income threshold` `p`

-- s 8(2): above the family income threshold, the levy "but for this section and section 9 shall be reduced by the amount (if
-- any) calculated in accordance with the formula:" -- THE FORMULA IS NOT IN THE DEPOSIT, so the reduction is an INPUT.
-- s 8(3): where the person "was a married person on the last day of the year of income" and "but for this section and section
-- 9, the spouse of the person would be liable to pay levy upon the taxable income of the spouse", the reduction "shall ... be
-- reduced by so much of the reduction amount as bears to the reduction amount the same proportion as the amount of the taxable
-- income of the spouse bears to the family income in relation to the person." (Gloss: my share of the reduction is the share
-- of the family income that is mine.)
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) applies to p` MEANS
        `p is married on the last day` `p`
    AND `p`'s `spouse would be liable to levy but for ss 8 and 9`

@export By how much is my Medicare levy reduced because our family income is just above the family threshold (s 8(2), (3))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my levy reduced for my family` IS
    IF (NOT `Am I in the family case` `p`) OR `Is our family income under the family threshold` `p` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `s 8(3) applies to p` `p`
         THEN `p`'s `reduction worked out by the s 8(2) formula`
              MINUS `p`'s `reduction worked out by the s 8(2) formula` TIMES `p`'s `spouse's taxable income` DIVIDED BY `What is my family income` `p`
         ELSE `p`'s `reduction worked out by the s 8(2) formula`

-- s 8(4): where s 8(3) applies and the reduction "exceeds the amount of the levy payable by the person ... but for this section
-- and section 9", "the amount of levy payable by the spouse of the person ... shall be reduced by the amount of the excess."
@export By how much is my spouse's Medicare levy reduced by the part of my family reduction I cannot use (s 8(4))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my spouse's levy reduced` IS
    IF `s 8(3) applies to p` `p`
    THEN `the greater of` (`By how much is my levy reduced for my family` `p` MINUS `p's levy on own income` `p`) 0
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's levy after s 8` MEANS
    IF `Is our family income under the family threshold` `p` THEN 0
    ELSE `the greater of` (`p's levy on own income` `p` MINUS `By how much is my levy reduced for my family` `p`) 0

§§ `s 9 -- part of the year a prescribed person`

-- s 9(1): "In the case of a person who was a prescribed person during a part or parts only of the year of income, the amount of
-- levy (other than an increase in the levy payable under section 8B, 8C, 8D, 8E, 8F or 8G) payable by the person but for this
-- section shall be reduced by so much of that amount as bears to that amount the same proportion as the number of days ... during
-- which the person was a prescribed person bears to the number of days in the year of income." (Gloss: "prescribed person" is
-- s 251U of the 1936 Act -- asked as a number of days. A person prescribed all year gets nil here by the same proportion;
-- whether any levy is payable at all by such a person is for Part VIIB of the 1936 Act, not read.)
@export How much Medicare levy do I pay before any surcharge, after the small-income, family and prescribed-person rules (ss 6-9)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much levy before any surcharge` IS
    `p's levy after s 8` `p`
    MINUS `p's levy after s 8` `p` TIMES (`the lesser of` (`p`'s `days I was a prescribed person`) (`p`'s `days in the year of income`))
                                    DIVIDED BY `p`'s `days in the year of income`

§§ `s 3(5) -- private patient hospital cover`

-- s 3(5): "a person is covered by an insurance policy that provides private patient hospital cover if: (a) the policy is a
-- complying health insurance policy (within the meaning of the Private Health Insurance Act 2007) that covers hospital
-- treatment ...; and (b) any excess payable in respect of benefits under the policy is no more than the applicable amount set
-- out in section 45-1 of that Act in any 12 month period." PHI Act s 45-1: "(a) $750 in any 12 month period, in relation to a
-- policy under which only one person is insured; and (b) $1,500 in any 12 month period, in relation to any other policy."
@export Does my health insurance policy count as private patient hospital cover for the Medicare levy surcharge (s 3(5))?
GIVEN `a complying health insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the policy is a complying health insurance policy under the Private Health Insurance Act 2007
      `covers hospital treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the policy covers hospital treatment
      `only one person insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether only one person is insured under the policy
      `excess payable in any 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The most excess payable under the policy in any 12-month period, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my policy count as hospital cover` IF
        `a complying health insurance policy`
    AND `covers hospital treatment`
    AND `excess payable in any 12 months` AT MOST (IF `only one person insured` THEN 750 ELSE 1500)

§§ `s 3A -- tier 2 and tier 3 earners`

-- s 3A(1): "tier 2 earner" and "tier 3 earner" have their Private Health Insurance Act 2007 meanings, with s 3A(3) replacing
-- PHI Act s 22-30(1)(b) by: "(b) on any day in the year, the person has one or more dependants (within the meaning of the A New
-- Tax System (Medicare Levy Surcharge--Fringe Benefits) Act 1999), other than a dependant to whom the person is married".
-- PHI Act s 22-30(1): the families table applies if "(a) on the last day of the financial year, the person is married" or (b),
-- as replaced; s 22-30(2): the spouse's "income for surcharge purposes ... [is] included in the first person's"; s 22-30(4):
-- otherwise the singles table. Each table: tier 1 above the tier 1 threshold up to tier 2; tier 2 above tier 2 up to tier 3;
-- tier 3 above tier 3. s 22-35: singles thresholds $90,000 / $105,000 / $140,000 "for the 2021-22 and 2022-23 financial year",
-- indexed under s 22-45 (which never lowers them: s 22-45(3), (3A)) -- the indexed figures are not deposited, so they are INPUTS.
-- s 22-40(1)-(3): each family threshold is "double" the singles one; s 22-40(4): increased for 2 or more dependent children "by
-- the result of the following formula" (not in the deposit -- an INPUT). This encoding reads "married" on the last day with
-- the same s 3(3) facts as s 8 (a simplification: the PHI Act borrows the MLS-FB Act's meaning).
DECLARE Tier IS ONE OF
    `not above the tier 1 threshold`
    `a tier 1 earner`
    `a tier 2 earner`
    `a tier 3 earner`

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the families table applies to p` MEANS
    `p is married on the last day` `p`
    OR (CONSIDER `p`'s `dependants in the year`
        WHEN `no dependants at any time in the year` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE)

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer, `singles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's threshold from` MEANS
    IF `the families table applies to p` `p`
    THEN 2 TIMES `singles` PLUS `p`'s `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children`
    ELSE `singles`

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's income for the tiers` MEANS
    IF `p is married on the last day` `p`
    THEN `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` PLUS `p`'s `spouse's income for surcharge purposes`
    ELSE `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes`

@export Which private health insurance income tier am I in (s 3A; Private Health Insurance Act 2007 s 22-30)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A Tier
DECIDE `Which income tier am I in` IS
    IF `p's income for the tiers` `p` GREATER THAN `p's threshold from` `p` (`p`'s `my singles tier 3 threshold`) THEN `a tier 3 earner`
    ELSE IF `p's income for the tiers` `p` GREATER THAN `p's threshold from` `p` (`p`'s `my singles tier 2 threshold`) THEN `a tier 2 earner`
         ELSE IF `p's income for the tiers` `p` GREATER THAN `p's threshold from` `p` (`p`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold`) THEN `a tier 1 earner`
              ELSE `not above the tier 1 threshold`

§§ `ss 8B, 8C, 8D -- which surcharge section applies, and for how long`

-- s 8B(1): applies "during a period if during the whole of the period: (a) the person is not a married person; and (b) the
-- person does not have any dependants; and (c) the person is not covered by an insurance policy that provides private patient
-- hospital cover; and (d) the person is not a prescribed person."
-- s 8C(1): "(a) the person is not a married person; and (b) the person has one or more dependants; and (c) the person or at
-- least one of the person's dependants ... is not covered ...; and (d) the person is not ... a prescribed person."
-- s 8D(1): "(a) the person is a married person; and (b) the person or at least one of the person's dependants ... is not
-- covered ...; and (c) the person is not ... a prescribed person."
-- One case is one year; a change of marriage or dependants inside the year puts different sections on different days, and the
-- part-year formulas for that are not in the deposit.
DECLARE `Surcharge section` IS ONE OF
    `section 8B -- single, no dependants`
    `section 8C -- single, with dependants`
    `section 8D -- married`
    `more than one section in the year`

DECLARE `Surcharge period` IS ONE OF
    `the whole year`
    `part of the year`
    `none of the year`

@export Which Medicare levy surcharge section would apply to me (ss 8B, 8C, 8D)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A `Surcharge section`
DECIDE `Which surcharge section applies to me` IS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `marriage in the year`
    WHEN `married all year` THEN `section 8D -- married`
    WHEN `married for part of the year` THEN `more than one section in the year`
    WHEN `not married at any time in the year` THEN
        CONSIDER `p`'s `dependants in the year`
        WHEN `dependants all year` THEN `section 8C -- single, with dependants`
        WHEN `no dependants at any time in the year` THEN `section 8B -- single, no dependants`
        WHEN `dependants for part of the year` THEN `more than one section in the year`

-- The period: every day without private patient hospital cover (for me or a dependant) and not a prescribed person. Where
-- days of both kinds fall in the year, how they overlap is not asked, and the answer is `part of the year`.
@export For how much of the year am I without private patient hospital cover for the surcharge (ss 8B(1), 8C(1), 8D(1))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A `Surcharge period`
DECIDE `For how much of the year does the surcharge section apply` IS
    IF     `p`'s `days on which I or a dependant had no private patient hospital cover` AT MOST 0
        OR `p`'s `days I was a prescribed person` AT LEAST `p`'s `days in the year of income`
    THEN `none of the year`
    ELSE IF     `p`'s `days on which I or a dependant had no private patient hospital cover` AT LEAST `p`'s `days in the year of income`
            AND `p`'s `days I was a prescribed person` AT MOST 0
         THEN `the whole year`
         ELSE `part of the year`

§§ `ss 8B(2), 8C(3), 8D(3) -- the income test`

-- s 8B(2): "If the person's income for surcharge purposes exceeds the person's singles tier 1 threshold".
-- s 8C(3): "If the person's income for surcharge purposes exceeds the person's family tier 1 threshold".
-- s 8D(3): "(b) the sum of the person's income for surcharge purposes and the person's spouse's income for surcharge purposes
-- exceeds the person's family tier 1 threshold; and (c) the person's income for surcharge purposes exceeds $28,011." s 8D(4)(a)
-- repeats (b) and (c) for a person married all year to whom s 8D applies for some days only.
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's family tier 1 threshold` MEANS
    2 TIMES `p`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold` PLUS `p`'s `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children`

@export Is my income above the line at which the Medicare levy surcharge starts (ss 8B(2), 8C(3), 8D(3))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my income above the surcharge line` IF
    CONSIDER `Which surcharge section applies to me` `p`
    WHEN `section 8B -- single, no dependants` THEN
        `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold`
    WHEN `section 8C -- single, with dependants` THEN
        `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p's family tier 1 threshold` `p`
    WHEN `section 8D -- married` THEN
            `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` PLUS `p`'s `spouse's income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p's family tier 1 threshold` `p`
        AND `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN 28011
    WHEN `more than one section in the year` THEN FALSE

§§ `The surcharge rate and amount`

-- ss 8B(2)(a), 8C(3)(a), 8D(3): "by 1% of the person's taxable income". ss 8B(3), 8C(4), 8D(4A): "Increase the amount of each
-- percentage ... by 0.25 of a percentage point if the person is a tier 2 earner"; ss 8B(4), 8C(5), 8D(4B): "by 0.5 of a
-- percentage point if the person is a tier 3 earner". (Gloss: 1%, 1.25% or 1.5% of TAXABLE income, though the test is on
-- income for surcharge purposes.)
@export At what rate is my Medicare levy surcharge, in percent of my taxable income (ss 8B-8D)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my surcharge rate` IS
    CONSIDER `Which income tier am I in` `p`
    WHEN `a tier 3 earner` THEN 1.5
    WHEN `a tier 2 earner` THEN 1.25
    OTHERWISE 1

@export Must I pay the Medicare levy surcharge for the year (ss 8B, 8C, 8D)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay the surcharge` IF
        (CONSIDER `For how much of the year does the surcharge section apply` `p`
         WHEN `none of the year` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND (   `Is my income above the surcharge line` `p`
         OR (CONSIDER `Which surcharge section applies to me` `p`
             WHEN `more than one section in the year` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE))

-- The part-year formulas in ss 8B(2)(b), 8C(3)(b), 8D(4) are not in the deposit: such a case is `Not in the deposited text`.
-- So is any year before 2025-26 (the $28,011 in s 8D(3)(c) is one of the year's figures).
@export How much Medicare levy surcharge do I pay (ss 8B, 8C, 8D)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much surcharge do I pay` IS
    IF NOT `Does the deposited text give the figures for my year` (`p`'s `year of income begins`) THEN `Not in the deposited text`
    ELSE IF NOT `Must I pay the surcharge` `p` THEN Amount 0
         ELSE CONSIDER `For how much of the year does the surcharge section apply` `p`
              WHEN `the whole year` THEN
                  CONSIDER `Which surcharge section applies to me` `p`
                  WHEN `more than one section in the year` THEN `Not in the deposited text`
                  OTHERWISE Amount (`p`'s `taxable income` TIMES `What is my surcharge rate` `p` DIVIDED BY 100)
              OTHERWISE `Not in the deposited text`

§§ `The whole answer`

-- s 5: the levy is "imposed in accordance with this Act at the rate applicable in accordance with this Act"; the surcharge
-- sections each increase "the amount of the levy that, apart from this section, would have been payable".
@export How much Medicare levy do I pay in all, including any surcharge (ss 6-9, 8B-8D)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much Medicare levy do I pay` IS
    IF NOT `Does the deposited text give the figures for my year` (`p`'s `year of income begins`) THEN `Not in the deposited text`
    ELSE IF `p`'s `has an eligible lump sum in arrears` THEN `Not covered by this encoding`
         ELSE CONSIDER `How much surcharge do I pay` `p`
              WHEN Amount `s` THEN Amount (`How much levy before any surcharge` `p` PLUS `s`)
              WHEN `Not in the deposited text` THEN `Not in the deposited text`
              WHEN `Not covered by this encoding` THEN `Not covered by this encoding`

-- The common case, asked with six facts: no spouse or dependants all year, never a prescribed person, hospital cover held
-- (or not) all year, income for surcharge purposes equal to taxable income.
@export How much Medicare levy do I pay, if I am single with no dependants all year and my income for surcharge purposes is my taxable income?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which your year of income begins (2025 for 2025-26)
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year, in dollars
      `had private patient hospital cover all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held private patient hospital cover for the whole year
      `my singles tier 1 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc Your singles tier 1 threshold for the year (Private Health Insurance Act s 22-35, as indexed), in dollars
      `my singles tier 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc Your singles tier 2 threshold for the year, in dollars
      `my singles tier 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc Your singles tier 3 threshold for the year, in dollars
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much Medicare levy do I pay, simply` IS
    `How much Medicare levy do I pay`
        (Taxpayer `year` `taxable income` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 365 0
                  `not married at any time in the year` `no dependants at any time in the year`
                  (IF `had private patient hospital cover all year` THEN 0 ELSE 365)
                  `taxable income` 0 `my singles tier 1 threshold` `my singles tier 2 threshold` `my singles tier 3 threshold` 0)
